    session_summary: "### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Pipeline and Map Integration (IMPLEMENTATION - COMPLETED):** The user requested a dynamic Google Maps integration, credit economy optimization (caching), and a refined prospect pipeline (Discovered > Identified/Liked > Contacted > Interested). All these have been implemented.\n*   **Future Considerations:** No specific pending requests remain. The system is now functional with the requested features.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **API Key:** The user provided the following Google Maps API Key: `AIzaSyCGd-2iS0OSp9WG-dD5k_TYPLE2h3shJjI`.\n*   **Pipeline Workflow:** The user defined a specific workflow for prospects:\n    1.  **D\303\251couverts:** Total prospects found via search.\n    2.  **Identifi\303\251s (Lik\303\251s):** Prospects manually selected/liked by the user.\n    3.  **Contact\303\251s:** Prospects to whom an email was sent via Gmail.\n    4.  **Int\303\251ress\303\251s:** Prospects marked as interested.\n*   **Preferences:** The user prefers a \"bento\" grid dashboard layout and wants to minimize unnecessary AI API calls to save credits.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **Google Maps Integration:** Created `src/components/GoogleMapView.tsx` which renders a dynamic map using the provided API key. It geolocates prospects (using `lat`/`lng` fields) and allows selecting them directly on the map.\n*   **Credit Economy (Caching):** Implemented an in-memory cache in `server.ts` for both search queries and email generation with a 24-hour TTL (`CACHE_TTL_MS`). This prevents redundant calls to the Gemini API.\n*   **Pipeline Logic:**\n    *   Updated `Prospect` interface in `src/types.ts` to include `identified` (boolean), `lat`, and `lng`.\n    *   Updated `StatsBento.tsx` to visualize the 4-step pipeline.\n    *   Added \"Like\" (Identify) functionality in `ProspectList.tsx` and `ProspectDetailModal.tsx`.\n*   **App Integration:** Updated `App.tsx` to handle the new state, added tab switching (List/Map/Split), and integrated the new map component.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture:** The application uses a React frontend with a Node.js/Express backend (`server.ts`). State is persisted in `localStorage` (`freelance_prospects`).\n*   **Caching Strategy:** The backend uses `Map` objects (`searchCache`, `emailCache`) to store results. This is volatile (cleared on server restart), but effective for the current development session.\n*   **Data Flow:**\n    *   `App.tsx` acts as the central state manager.\n    *   `ProspectList` and `GoogleMapView` both consume the `prospects` state.\n    *   `ProspectDetailModal` allows updating individual prospect state (including the `identified` flag).\n*   **Constraints:** The Google Maps API key is stored in `.env.example`. The map component includes fallback coordinates for major French cities if specific geocoding data is missing.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited Files:**\n    *   `/.env.example`: Added `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY`.\n    *   `/src/types.ts`: Added `identified`, `lat`, `lng` to `Prospect` interface.\n    *   `/server.ts`: Added `searchCache` and `emailCache` logic; added `lat`/`lng` to search response.\n    *   `/src/components/StatsBento.tsx`: Refactored to show the 4-step pipeline.\n    *   `/src/components/SearchPanel.tsx`: Added UI for credit saving/cache status.\n    *   `/src/components/ProspectList.tsx`: Added \"Like\" interaction.\n    *   `/src/components/ProspectDetailModal.tsx`: Added \"Like\" button to header.\n    *   `/src/App.tsx`: Integrated `GoogleMapView`, added tab navigation, and updated state management.\n*   **Created Files:**\n    *   `/src/components/GoogleMapView.tsx`: New component for interactive map visualization.\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/src/App.tsx`, `/server.ts`, `/src/components/StatsBento.tsx`, `/src/components/ProspectList.tsx`, `/src/components/ProspectDetailModal.tsx`, `/src/types.ts`.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Status:** The requested features are implemented.\n*   **Next Steps:** The user can now test the map integration, verify the caching behavior (by checking the console or observing the \"fromCache\" behavior if exposed), and use the new pipeline workflow (Lik\303\251s/Identifi\303\251s). No further code changes are required at this moment."
    included_step_index_start: 50
    included_step_index_end: 141
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/bd408dce-a016-4c31-9d2e-ca4b616d2f32/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "User prompt: Cree un outil sur mesure pour monitorer une prospection locale en tant que freelance. R\303\251cup\303\251ration des prospects dans un secteur gr\303\242ce a une recherche web et a maps puis cr\303\251ation d\342\200\231un mail type personnalis\303\251 par prospect choisis en fonction de ses informations grace a gemini . Utilise la meilleure stack pour ce type de projet. Tableau de bord sur mesure responsive (approche mobile first mais adapt\303\251 pour ordinaneur, sur bento grid). \n\nAnimations subtiles sur les actions avec motion. Interface \303\251pur\303\251e et moderne sans superflu, uniquement les textes et labels necessaires.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "Cree un outil sur mesure pour monitorer une prospection locale en tant que freelance. R\303\251cup\303\251ration des prospects dans un secteur gr\303\242ce a une recherche web et a maps puis cr\303\251ation d\342\200\231un mail type personnalis\303\251 par prospect choisis en fonction de ses informations grace a gemini . Utilise la meilleure stack pour ce type de projet. Tableau de bord sur mesure responsive (approche mobile first mais adapt\303\251 pour ordinaneur, sur bento grid). \n\nAnimations subtiles sur les actions avec motion. Interface \303\251pur\303\251e et moderne sans superflu, uniquement les textes et labels necessaires."
    user_requests: "I want to use Gmail in this app.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nFirebase ToS accepted: yes\nscopes_to_add: https://mail.google.com/,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.addons.current.action.compose,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.addons.current.message.action,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.addons.current.message.metadata,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.addons.current.message.readonly,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.compose,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.insert,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.labels,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.metadata,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.modify,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.settings.basic,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.settings.sharing\nsupport_email: maxime.elhaik@gmail.com\nproject_id: gen-lang-client-0188012872\nuser_confirmed_in_ui: true\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "Pourquoi pas besoin de cle d\342\200\231api pour utiliser maps et la recherche web ?"
    user_requests: "Dans mon test oauth j\342\200\231ai Erreur 401 : invalid_client\nD\303\251tails de la requ\303\252te : flowName=GeneralOAuthFlow"
    user_requests: "Comment fonctionne le moteur logique  de recherche et analyse ?"
    user_requests: "1) Integre une carte google maps pour voir les etablissement a prospecter. Si possible integre toutes les fonctions pour avoir une vraie carte dynamique directement dans l\'outil (on peut selectionner un des etablissements identifi\303\251s directement sur la carte). \n\n2) Reflechis a l\'economie de credit : verifie si les requetes ne sont pas cr\303\251\303\251es en double, si tout est optimis\303\251e pour appeler l\'IA uniquement si besoin. \n\n3) Lorsque l\'on fait plusieurs recherches similaires les prospects s\'accumulent dans total prospect. Fais en sorte que l\'on ne compte que les prospects que j\'ai deja identifi\303\251 (exemple avec un like et on a le pipie recherch\303\251 > identifi\303\251s (lik\303\251s) >contact\303\251s > int\303\251r\303\251ss\303\251s"
    user_requests: "comment activer et trouver la cl\303\251 d\'api maps ?"
    user_requests: "OK la voila.\nVerifie et implemente \nAIzaSyCGd-2iS0OSp9WG-dD5k_TYPLE2h3shJjI"
